<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic32ea4ffd77d58263c901f0d4d896957e556c10b" commit="34c126f36fd17694debc9a9b619899d639a699d9" commit_message="libpayload: Remove configs with no coreboot equivalent    $ cd ~/trunk/src/third_party/chromiumos-overlay/sys-boot/coreboot   $ ls ../libpayload/files/configs/config.* | while read n     do       if [ ! -r files/configs/$(basename $n) ]; then         git rm $n       fi     done  Signed-off-by: Stefan Reinauer &lt;reinauer@google.com&gt;  BRANCH=none TEST=no functional difference BUG=none  Change-Id: Ic32ea4ffd77d58263c901f0d4d896957e556c10b Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/600772 Commit-Ready: Stefan Reinauer &lt;reinauer@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Stefan Reinauer &lt;reinauer@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Martin Roth &lt;martinroth@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="600772" owner_email="reinauer@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/72/600772/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If13acb5e2dff6148cd3561266aa979b054e4b6d0" commit="b08243df5bfbb2b0f22e58b1433fcb8adba2150a" commit_message="Unify / simplify libpayload config files again  In Ib8a9da52b6b889a5c12e80767f555893bfdf3753 we unified and simplified all libpayload config files. Since then, a few changes occured, so redo this:    $ cd ~/trunk/src/third_party/coreboot/payloads/libpayload   $ for i in ~/trunk/src/third_party/chromiumos-overlay/sys-boot/libpayload/files/configs/config.*     do       cp $i .config; make savedefconfig       mv defconfig $i     done   $  BRANCH=none BUG=none TEST=manual inspection of config files  Change-Id: If13acb5e2dff6148cd3561266aa979b054e4b6d0 Signed-off-by: Stefan Reinauer &lt;reinauer@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/601089 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="601089" owner_email="reinauer@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/89/601089/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8a8c0d2cd5c460c9f72d349f7ed158c6c4a597bf" commit="47d28514353d0ee71e244d26ea309720089ce672" commit_message="Reland &quot;port-mbim: use the mbim-proxy by default&quot;  This reverts commit 876e6dfdf4c84961a00e3f909d995a9716b899fe.  Using mbim-proxy will make things somewhat more resilient if users of the MBIM port fail to clean up, e.g. if ModemManager crashes. It would also allow multiple users of the MBIM port at the same time (so users of mbimcli could pass -p and interact with a modem at the same time as MM, for instance).  BUG=chromium:740724 TEST=unit tests, manual testing on device; verify that mbim-proxy   is running as the modem user and we are still able to send and   receive messages on /dev/cdc-wdm0  Change-Id: I8a8c0d2cd5c460c9f72d349f7ed158c6c4a597bf Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/568908 Commit-Ready: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="568908" owner_email="ejcaruso@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/modemmanager-next" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/modemmanager-next" ref="refs/changes/08/568908/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6e3e0a200262de7eb80e4236058b02b5d524d0ac" commit="1af2263e06f4d4295250f73099626dcd77115fdd" commit_message="dev-lang/go: Cherry-pick parse-old-tar.patch for Go 1.8  This cherry-picks https://golang.org/cl/53635 for dev-lang/go package.  Note that the original commit includes an binary file for testing purpose, which can not be patched through epatch. So I just deleted it as well as the test code.  BUG=b:64542183 TEST='emerge cross-x86_64-cros-linux-gnu/go'  Change-Id: I6e3e0a200262de7eb80e4236058b02b5d524d0ac Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/614388 Commit-Ready: Ke Wu &lt;mikewu@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Ke Wu &lt;mikewu@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Rahul Chaudhry &lt;rahulchaudhry@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="614388" owner_email="mikewu@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/88/614388/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie2bb141c72252aee98e4cd4a284a01b4d57605f4" commit="59b01aec14142f6ede514cc711014925c8286765" commit_message="scarlet: Remap DMA channels for USART1  To enable console with DMA, we need to specifically remap DMA channels for USART1.  ch2/3 and ch6/7 are already used by SPI1/2 modules. So we have to remap USART1_TX to ch4 and USART1_RX to ch5.  BUG=b:64575809 BRANCH=none TEST=confirm ec console works on scarlet rev1  Change-Id: Ie2bb141c72252aee98e4cd4a284a01b4d57605f4 Signed-off-by: Philip Chen &lt;philipchen@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/611147 Commit-Ready: Philip Chen &lt;philipchen@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Philip Chen &lt;philipchen@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="611147" owner_email="philipchen@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/47/611147/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I40d55191e40f5bb6794655af1f3587751584f9fa" commit="c62b2b8511f8d091906404c47bed1c6cd7332eea" commit_message="CHROMIUM: Remove dragon_defconfig  This references the now-deleted bcmdhd driver, and is not being maintained anyway.  BUG=chromium:748301 TEST=trybots  Change-Id: I40d55191e40f5bb6794655af1f3587751584f9fa Signed-off-by: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/590809 Commit-Ready: Kirtika Ruchandani &lt;kirtika@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kirtika Ruchandani &lt;kirtika@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kirtika Ruchandani &lt;kirtika@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="590809" owner_email="cernekee@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/09/590809/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id799c505ba65882a9b65c52d48979182c42b22a4" commit="eead367fc4d9d9cb229d67991bc74d544655e3fe" commit_message="platform_FilePerms: allow /sys/fs/pstore too  Depending on the system, pstore might be mounted at the old /dev/pstore path, or the new /sys/fs/pstore path.  Allow them both.  BUG=chromium:755343 TEST=precq passes  Change-Id: Id799c505ba65882a9b65c52d48979182c42b22a4 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/616000 Commit-Ready: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Jorge Lucangeli Obes &lt;jorgelo@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="616000" owner_email="vapier@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/00/616000/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id417203ebbda06178466211bf95e8720479fe0b1" commit="c55dfd42f44424488c9144d8b4eb92a9d431fa10" commit_message="Remove unused Disconnect method in BluetoothHIDFlow  This method does not appear to be used, and has a name collision with code in the RN42 class, which we do use.  Flip the method resolution order in BluetoothHIDMouseFlow, so that if this conflict happens again, we'll be more likely to catch it when editing the BluetoothHIDMouse hierarchy.  Added a note to help remind future readers that this functionality exists in case it becomes relevant, as other flows seem to use it.  BUG=chromium:752719 TEST=Run this code on the Chameleon board: $ make &amp;&amp; make remote-install CHAMELEON_HOST=$CHAMELEON_IP Execute the non-flaky non-stress tests that use this code, and watch them pass: $ test_that --board ${BOARD} --args &quot;chameleon_host=${CHAMELEON_IP}&quot; \ ${DUT_IP} bluetooth_AdapterPairing.mouse \ bluetooth_AdapterPairing.mouse.pairing_twice \ bluetooth_AdapterHIDReports.mouse  Change-Id: Id417203ebbda06178466211bf95e8720479fe0b1 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/609684 Commit-Ready: Alexander Lent &lt;alent@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Alexander Lent &lt;alent@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Wai-Hong Tam &lt;waihong@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Miao-chen Chou &lt;mcchou@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="609684" owner_email="alent@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/chameleon" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/chameleon" ref="refs/changes/84/609684/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="9844.0.0-rc4"/></manifest>